# tiberius: the strata engine's local patch, against upstream ffa80d73 (v0.2.10, engine 0.1.56).
# REBASED 2026-11-03 onto ffa80d73.  Two hunk conflicts in generate.cpp, both resolved by keeping both
# sides: upstream's new `keep_sync()` at the request-ending pin release (it waits on the idle drafter's
# queued upkeep, so the pins are released after it), and the `use_mtp` -> `draft_on` rename in the
# `drafted` guard, where our refill-timing join is kept around upstream's variable.  Everything else
# applied cleanly.  0.2.10's expert_source changes (the ArenaExpertSource #4846 RAM fallback and the
# Windows standby-list release) sit outside this patch's FileExpertSource region, and the ggml pin is
# unchanged (third_party/ggml/VERSION.txt), so nothing under third_party/ggml moved.
#
# ADDED 2026-11-04: change 3 (the transactional park) was written on top of that rebase; park_source()
# and conversation_cache.hpp are outside every region changes 1-2 touch (the cache header was not in
# this patch before it), so it needs no merge.  The whole patch was regenerated against ffa80d73 and
# re-applied in order onto a pristine tree (byte-identical result; transcript in
# /tmp/strata-tune/park-patch.md).  Code-only so far: the build and the isolated-harness probe are
# task-7, not run yet.
#
# Three changes, in one patch because changes 1-2 interleave in the same regions of
# expert_source.{hpp,cpp}, prefill.{hpp,cpp} and generate.cpp; change 3 is independent (one function in
# generate.cpp, two methods in conversation_cache.hpp).  Changes 1-2 are local and opt-in through their
# own env var - nothing they add runs unless the module sets it.  Change 3 is always on and only changes
# what a REFUSED park does: an admitted park behaves exactly as before.
#
# 1. STRATA_REGISTER_DAX, the sliding DAX window.  cudaHostRegister cannot pin
#    the 46.84 GiB pack (the driver caps a process's total registered host memory
#    at ~7 GiB, measured), so the engine registers a 6 GiB window of whole
#    page-aligned layers over the mmap'd pack and slides it as the prefill walk
#    advances; every layer the window holds is DMA-able straight out of DAX, which
#    removes the CPU staging path.  Measured 2026-10-02 on the real corpus:
#    prefill 12,325 -> 9,527 ms (-22.7%) for a 4292-token prompt.
#    STRATA_REGISTER_DAX_MIB is the window budget (6144 is the measured ceiling:
#    6912 registers and 7168 is refused, so the 8 rotations per prompt are
#    irreducible).
# 2. STRATA_REFILL_PIN_SRC, the decode-time VRAM refill read from registered
#    sources: the adaptive tier's 2 MiB copies were 98% pageable at ~0.87 ms each
#    and sat on the decode loop's critical path.  The patch resolves a batch's
#    sources first, merges their page-rounded spans, registers them (ReadOnly |
#    Portable) and releases them once the batch's event has landed.  Measured
#    2026-10-02, counterbalanced, 8 runs/arm: decode +12.2% / +7.1% / +5.9% on
#    three cells, refill join 18.04 -> 1.46 ms per window.
# 3. The transactional park (park_source, generate.cpp).  The physical-RAM admission gate used to run
#    `while (!admit() && ... evict_oldest())` BEFORE it knew whether the park could be admitted, so a
#    REFUSED park had already evicted up to slots() parked conversations (production: "need 994 MiB plus
#    384 MiB floor, 1102 MiB available; evicted 2, 0 still parked" - two good conversations destroyed by
#    a park that never happened; 126 refusals in one 8 h run, 893 in the log), and the retained-K/V donor
#    (take_reuse_for) was consumed by the same refusal.  Now the gate is checked ONCE before make_room()
#    and before any eviction, against available + the bytes every evictable parked conversation would
#    return (ConversationCache::evictable_bytes); a park that could not fit even with the cache emptied
#    is skipped with "nothing evicted, N still parked" and the donor is handed back
#    (ConversationCache::give_reuse).  A park that CAN fit takes the old eviction loop unchanged; its
#    refusal is now reachable only when RAM changed between the pre-check and the loop.  No upstream
#    counterpart: #4677 fixes a different, HIP-only stop-bound park bug (see default.nix).
#
# Two hardening pieces ride with the pin, both needed by this box:
#   * the straddle guard: a span that PARTLY overlaps an existing registration is
#     dropped, not registered (the driver refuses a copy whose source begins inside
#     one registration and ends outside it), and a refused exchange staging drops
#     that swap instead of failing the request (upstream aborts).
#   * the register/unregister bookkeeping is per request, so no pin outlives it.
#
# REBASED 2026-10-27 onto 5e8a4cca (v0.2.7).  Upstream rewrote the adaptive refill
# between 0.2.4.2 and 0.2.7 (the "resolve every swap first" plans pass, the
# nib::guard_raw instrumentation, the batch H2D path), so the two largest hunks
# were re-merged by hand: the plans pass now carries our pin classification
# (BlobClass) and the batch registration, and upstream's nib guard is kept inside
# our loop.  The serve path and the generate path each carry a copy, as before.

